  "coverage": "Twelve European provinces and 342 municipalities (GISCO 2024), plus all six Dutch Caribbean jurisdictions with focused island entry. All six Dutch Caribbean jurisdictions: Aruba, Curaçao and Sint Maarten (constituent countries), and Bonaire, Sint Eustatius and Saba (Caribbean public bodies). No European province or administrative subdivision is fabricated for these islands. Full OSM land coastlines are clipped to the verified administrative relation, excluding territorial sea. All six open the Netherlands page directly at the selected island.",
  "processing": "All subdivisions use the shared regional renderer. Parent polygons are dissolved from one municipal topology; shared internal edges are stored once. Geometry is simplified together to about 33 m north-south after the source generalisation. Deeper levels load per parent. Land frontiers retain the existing France/Italy reference where present and are drawn once; reference border lines cross large lakes and sea channels independently of coastlines. Population retains the original reference date; no GDP values are inferred.",
